  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1201 PM CST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nWe continue our quiet weather pattern through the first half of the \nlong term with a continued warmup into the low to mid 70s expected. \nHowever, what was looking like a somewhat wetter weekend has since \nwaned with most global models indicating a drier trend across the \nboard. Moisture that was associated with the front seems unlikely to \nmake it far enough into our area and thus remains trapped across S \nTexas instead. Regardless we still do have some low end pops (20-\n30%) across are far southern areas that could see some of this \nmoisture result in a few showers Sunday into Sunday evening. \n\nOtherwise looking ahead Eventually the upper level low progresses \neastward across the TX panhandle and sends a cold front down into \nour area next Monday as the southern sub tropical jet continues \nnudging northward causing more influence across southern and south \ncentral TX. Models continue to diverge on how and when this pattern \ndevelops but looking ahead it does look like for now our area will \nbecome much more active as disturbances ride just to the north of \nthis feature impacting the Thanksgiving Holiday week ahead. For \nthose that have travel plans be sure to keep an eye on the forecast \nas we continue to get closer to next week.",
